msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Max Auto-tune Example\n"
"\n"
"This example demonstrates how to use the `max_autotune` parameter in `torch.compile` to automatically select the optimal configuration for a given model and hardware. `max_autotune` will perform extensive performance tuning during compilation, which may increase compilation time but can significantly improve inference performance.\n"
"\n"
"## Key Points\n"
"\n"
"- `max_autotune=True` enables automatic tuning of convolution algorithms, matrix multiplication algorithms, and other operators.\n"
"- During the tuning process, multiple candidate implementations are tested to select the fastest one.\n"
"- This parameter is particularly useful for models that require high performance, such as large language models or computer vision models.\n"
"- Note that enabling `max_autotune` will increase compilation time, especially on the first run.\n"
"\n"
"## Code Example\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch.nn as nn\n"
"import time\n"
"\n"
"# Define a simple model\n"
"class SimpleModel(nn.Module):\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__()\n"
"        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(784, 256)\n"
"        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(256, 128)\n"
"        self.fc3 = nn.Linear(128, 10)\n"
"        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n"
"\n"
"    def forward(self, x):\n"
"        x = self.relu(self.fc1(x))\n"
"        x = self.relu(self.fc2(x))\n"
"        x = self.fc3(x)\n"
"        return x\n"
"\n"
"# Create model and input\n"
"model = SimpleModel().cuda()\n"
"input_tensor = torch.randn(64, 784).cuda()\n"
"\n"
"# Compile with max_autotune\n"
"compiled_model = torch.compile(model, mode=\"max-autotune\")\n"
"\n"
"# Warm up\n"
"for _ in range(10):\n"
"    output = compiled_model(input_tensor)\n"
"\n"
"# Measure inference time\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"start_time = time.time()\n"
"for _ in range(100):\n"
"    output = compiled_model(input_tensor)\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"end_time = time.time()\n"
"\n"
"print(f\"Average inference time with max_autotune: {(end_time - start_time) / 100 * 1000:.2f} ms\")\n"
"\n"
"# Compare with non-compiled model\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"start_time = time.time()\n"
"for _ in range(100):\n"
"    output = model(input_tensor)\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"end_time = time.time()\n"
"\n"
"print(f\"Average inference time without compilation: {(end_time - start_time) / 100 * 1000:.2f} ms\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Notes\n"
"\n"
"1. `max_autotune` may require additional GPU memory for storing tuning results.\n"
"2. For small models, the compilation overhead may outweigh the performance gains.\n"
"3. It is recommended to use `max_autotune` in production environments where inference performance is critical.\n"

msgid "max_autotune 使用示例"
msgstr "max_autotune usage example"

msgid "`max_autotune` 是 Triton-Ascend 提供的增强自动调优装饰器，旨在简化多参数调优的代码编写。与社区版 `autotune` 要求用户手动枚举所有 `triton.Config` 不同，`max_autotune` 允许用户仅提供少量基础配置（如分块大小），并自动将相关的编译器选项（如 `num_stages`、`enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance` 等）纳入最优组合的搜索空间。用户也可以通过参数列表显式控制搜索范围。"
msgstr "`max_autotune` is an enhanced auto-tuning decorator provided by Triton-Ascend, designed to simplify the code writing for multi-parameter tuning. Unlike the community version of `autotune`, which requires users to manually enumerate all `triton.Config` instances, `max_autotune` allows users to provide only a small set of base configurations (such as block sizes) and automatically incorporates relevant compiler options (such as `num_stages`, `enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance`, etc.) into the search space for the optimal combination. Users can also explicitly control the search scope through a parameter list."

msgid "**适用场景**：Ascend NPU 上的 `cube`、`mix`、`vector` 算子，尤其适合需要同时调整多个硬件相关参数的场景。"
msgstr "**Applicable Scenarios**: `cube`, `mix`, and `vector` operators on Ascend NPU, especially suitable for scenarios where multiple hardware-related parameters need to be adjusted simultaneously."

msgid "基本使用示例"
msgstr "Basic usage example"

msgid "以下示例演示了使用 `max_autotune` 对一个简单的向量加法 kernel 进行自动调优。与社区版 `autotune` 相比，`max_autotune` 还会自动将不同的编译器选项纳入调优空间，无需用户手动指定。"
msgstr "The following example demonstrates using `max_autotune` to automatically tune a simple vector addition kernel. Compared to the community edition's `autotune`, `max_autotune` also automatically includes different compiler options in the tuning space, without requiring the user to specify them manually."

msgid "import torch\\n"
msgstr "import torch"

msgid "进阶使用：精确控制调优参数"
msgstr "Advanced Usage: Precisely Controlling Tuning Parameters"

msgid "用户可以通过 **tuning_params 显式指定需要调优的编译器选项及其取值列表；未指定的参数会使用内置默认值。以下示例展示了如何对多个参数进行组合搜索。"
msgstr "Users can explicitly specify the compiler options to be tuned and their value lists via **tuning_params; unspecified parameters will use built-in default values. The following example demonstrates how to perform a combined search over multiple parameters."

msgid "from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune\\n"
msgstr "from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune"
